{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nBug tickets carry no record of WHICH detection channel found them (canary, CI, review bot, human audit, user report), so escape-channel trends are unmeasurable. Retroactive classification was rejected (unreliable); capture must happen at creation with zero added user friction.\n\n## Approach\nAutomated filers set an environment variable (e.g. REBAR_DETECTED_BY=canary|ci|review-bot) that 'rebar create' reads and stamps into the create event; scales to client projects because the filer owns its own env. Human/agent sources may pass an OPTIONAL '--detected-by <source>' flag; absent both, the field is simply unset (never required, never prompted). Document the flag in agent guidance and the bug-creation contract (see canary-hardening sibling).\n\nValidation policy (deterministic, never blocks filing): the value is a free-form token, normalized by strip() + lowercase. Empty or whitespace-only after strip -> treated as unset (field absent from the event). Any non-empty normalized value is stamped verbatim — there is NO enforced enum; the vocabulary canary|ci|review-bot|agent|human-audit|user-report is documented as the recommended set (the metrics lens buckets unknown tokens under 'other'), so new channels never require a code change and create never fails on the value.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/create.py (or the create command module): read env var + optional flag\n- event schema: optional detected_by field on create events (additive, reducer-tolerated)\n- docs: config/env-vars registry entry + agent guidance line\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: env var set -> field present in event and shown by 'rebar show'. Flag overrides env. Edge: neither set -> field absent, create unchanged. Validation rows: empty string / whitespace-only -> field absent, create succeeds; mixed-case with padding (' Canary ') -> stamped as 'canary'; unknown token ('fuzzer') -> stamped verbatim, create succeeds.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] REBAR_DETECTED_BY env var stamps detected_by on created tickets; --detected-by flag overrides; absence changes nothing.\n- [ ] Normalization is strip+lowercase; empty/whitespace-only is treated as unset; unknown tokens are stamped verbatim (no enum enforcement); create never fails on the value.\n- [ ] Field is additive: existing stores/reducers tolerate events without it; no migration required.\n- [ ] Registered in the env-var/docs registry so the drift gate covers it.\n- [ ] Tests cover env, flag, absence, precedence, and the validation rows (empty, whitespace, mixed-case+padding, unknown token).\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785711071169275001,"uuid":"52220691-2813-45e1-89c6-5a2738c11094"}